= Steward Conference Leaked

Axton's former police chief and <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> member Albert Grenshaw, who's also apart of our executive committee, has brought a report received from an informant about a meeting of <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> regional officials. The discussions is of what would happen if the elections were to bring a <span style="color: #7A3C00;">far</span>-<span style="color: #3E88B3;">right</span> majority; an immediate state of emergency, suspension of parts of the constitution, non-secret supervised balloting, all with the support of the Defense Minister Staal.

If a majority isn't received, the alternative would be to pit the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Loyalists**</span> and Staal's Commonwealth Army against Goodryke, and if Goodryke refused to act, they would be forced to take action themselves.

- @Sovereigntist

@Sovereigntist
title: Immediately strengthen the Banners in response.
subtitle: -1 resource
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
choose-if: resources >= 1
on-arrival: royalist_urgency += 1; resources -= 1; banner_strength += 200; banner_militancy += 0.05

This development has persuaded the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> leadership—and Joran Vesh himself—to grant the Banners independent authority and financial support, which its leaders deem essential.

Such backing is especially critical following our loss of Heartland and its well-equipped police force.